                    "user_profile": {
                      "name": "Ditsy Mitzi",
                      "avatar": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/67f7b9ea-1d14-4867-9130-6acb678e3caa._CR62%2C0%2C375%2C375_SX460_SX48_.jpg",
                      "url": "https://amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AELHQKVUIQ55MNTGQCRRLCLAQ3HQ?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
                      "reviews_count": null,
                      "locations": "US"
                    },
                    "title": "Helped After My Appendectomy",
                    "url": "https://amazon.com/portal/customer-reviews/srp/-/R1Y4NUXMJJ0X8N/ref=cm_cr_dp_d_rvw_ttl?_encoding=UTF8&ie=UTF8",
                    "review_text": "I’ve always had an issue with having regular bowel movements so in order not to be constipated (cuz let’s be real, constipation can be very painful) I try to take these stool softener on a daily basis. Sometimes I forget to take them but normally I’m pretty good about it. Last year, on a cold November night I was awoken with pain in my abdomen. It was the kind of pain that makes you take notice and doesn’t let you fall asleep. At first I thought it could be cramps or even constipation but even after taking a laxative (not a stool softener) this pain would not go away. I briefly considered it might be my appendix but since I didn’t have chills, fever or nausea I dismissed that idea from my brain. I wish I didn’t because 24 hrs later I ended up in the emergency room having surgery on an “acute” perforated appendix. While at the hospital they loaded me up on antibiotics and pain medication which ironically caused me to be constipated. Now for anyone whose had surgery, you know that to have a bowel movement will now be very painful. I’m glad the doctors and nurses recommended that I take a stool softener because with all the meds I was taking and all the pain I was in I might have forgotten to take it. After having my appendix removed at old age of 52 and suffering  a subsequent wound infection because of my appendix I am now religiously taking at least 2 of these a day. After the surgery I did purchase the Colace at CVS because my doctor recommended it but I’ve since gone back to using these and have not noticed a change in effectiveness. I have however noticed a change in my wallet. Lol. PS.  Moral of the story is this…. If you have pain in your abdomen for more than 8 hours then take yourself to the hospital. Don’t wait for almost 24 hours like I did. If I had waited longer I might not be alive to write this review. Also if your bowel movements are irregular, it wouldn’t hurt to pop one of these pills daily to help in that area. I know it has helped me. 😍😍😍",
