                    "review_text": "UPDATE MAY 2016- you may need to take a stool softener .  i recommend generic colace (docusate sodium).  i have bought the kirkland brand in bottles of 400 and a generic bottle of 1,000 by Ready InCase_  looking @ the label i discovered both brands are distributed by the same company_PL Developments, out of Westbury NY__if U buy 1,000 of name brand-could cost $200 instead of $20 for generic Kirkland Signature Stool Softener Docusate Sodium 100 mg, 400 Softgels/Bottle Gericare Stool Softener Docusate Sodium 1000 Softgels, Compares to Colace, 100 mg each if you are buying a stool softener, you may also need a stimulant laxative_ i recommend Major (or any generic) bisacodyl._ the name brand is Dulcolax. f i bought the name brand Dulcolax_ with the same active ingredient of bisacodyl_ 1,000 tabs would cost $200 instead of $9-$10 the bottle i bought on April 2016 has a  'use by'  date of August 2018_ 2 1/3 year shelf life.  so, don't have to worry about expiring. Bisacodyl Tablets 5 Mg 1000 i've been buying these generic versions from Amazon for 12 years and never had a problem. ----------- OLD 2013 review_(They are stool softeners- and they do soften my stool. The price was much more reasonable than the drug store or super market. They don't expire until sometime in 2013 so there's plenty of time to use them.) ---------- I highly recommend these generic stool softeners and stimulant laxatives_ i take medicine that forces me to need to take these regularly- and am grateful i can get them for $10-$20 instead of $80-$200 (1,000 of the name brand bisacodyl would cost $200) i will include pics of the bottles- labels- tablets_ i hope some of what i shared was helpful 2 U_ thanks",
